cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. It is a preprint and has not been peer reviewed."
title: "Consecutive eighth-power residues: Lambda(8,2) = 1508324"
abstract: >-
  A computer-assisted proof that Lambda(8,2) = 1508324 (OEIS A000445, term k = 8; Erdős problem #436):
  an explicit 74-exception exponent vector whose first pair of consecutive zeros is (1508324, 1508325),
  realised by infinitely many primes by a theorem of Mills (1963), together with a re-certification of
  the known upper bound (Reble 2019; Arevalo 2026). Includes the certificates, vectors, checkers and a
  verification script. The proofs, programs and text were produced with an AI system (Claude, by Anthropic) under the author's direction, and no person has verified the proofs or the code; see the README.
authors:
